'''''Pilea involucrata''''' (Sims) Urb., commonly known as the '''friendship plant''',<ref>{{Cite web |title=Pilea involucrata (Sims) C.H.Wright & Dewar {{!}} Plants of the World Online {{!}} Kew Science |url=http://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:77091436-1 |access-date=2024-05-20 |website=Plants of the World Online |language=en}}</ref> is a species of flowering plant in the [[Urticaceae|nettle family Urticaceae]], native to [[Central and South America]].<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=Pilea involucrata - Plant Finder |url=http://www.missouribotanicalgarden.org/PlantFinder/PlantFinderDetails.aspx?taxonid=287427&isprofile=0&basic=%25 |access-date=2024-05-20 |website=www.missouribotanicalgarden.org}}</ref> It is a popular [[houseplant]] due to its unique foliage and relatively easy care.<ref name=":0" /> This species is best known for its popular [[cultivar]], ''Pilea involucrata'' 'Moon Valley'.

== Description ==
''Pilea involucrata'' is a bushy, trailing plant typically growing to a height and spread of {{convert|10|–|12|in|cm|abbr=off}}.<ref>{{Cite web |title=How to Grow and Care for Pilea Involucrata |url=https://www.thespruce.com/pilea-involucrata-plant-profile-7374044 |access-date=2024-05-20 |website=The Spruce |language=en}}</ref> The species typically features bright green leaves with a quilted or corrugated texture, often with bronze or reddish undersides.<ref name=":1">{{Cite web |title=Pilea involucrata (Friendship Plant) |url=https://www.gardenia.net/plant/pilea-involucrata-friendship-plant-grwo-care-tips |access-date=2024-05-20 |website=www.gardenia.net}}</ref> It occasionally produces small, pink-white flowers, but these are infrequent when grown indoors.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.shootgardening.com/plants/pilea-involucrata |access-date=2024-05-20 |website=www.shootgardening.com}}</ref>

== Cultivation ==
The friendship plant prefers bright, indirect light and well-draining soil that is kept evenly moist.<ref name=":1" /> It thrives in temperatures between {{convert|65|–|80|F|C}} and moderate to high humidity levels.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Pilea Production Guide |url=https://mrec.ifas.ufl.edu/foliage/folnotes/pilea.htm |access-date=2024-05-20 |website=mrec.ifas.ufl.edu}}</ref> ''Pilea involucrata'' is easily [[Plant propagation|propagated]] through division or stem cuttings.

== Cultivar: 'Moon Valley' ==
''Pilea involucrata'' 'Moon Valley', also known as the Moon Valley plant, is a distinct [[cultivar]] recognized for its deeply textured, cratered leaves that resemble the moon's surface.<ref>{{Cite web |title=How to care for the Moon Valley Pilea {{!}} Plants 101 |url=https://www.thesill.com/blog/how-to-care-for-moon-valley-pilea-pilea-mollis |access-date=2024-05-20 |website=The Sill |language=en}}</ref> The foliage is primarily chartreuse-green, highlighted by prominent bronze-colored veins. It is often mistakenly identified as ''[[Pilea mollis]]'' due to its similar appearance and the shared common name "friendship plant".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Rae |title=Pilea involucrata: A Complete Guide to the Friendship Plant |url=https://terrariumtribe.com/terrarium-plants/pilea-involucrata-friendship-plant/ |access-date=2024-05-20 |website=Terrarium Tribe |language=en-GB}}</ref>

== Uses ==
''Pilea involucrata'', including its 'Moon Valley' cultivar, is primarily grown as a [[houseplant]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Pilea involucrata (Friendship Plant, Panamiga) {{!}} North Carolina Extension Gardener Plant Toolbox |url=https://plants.ces.ncsu.edu/plants/pilea-involucrata/ |access-date=2024-05-20 |website=plants.ces.ncsu.edu}}</ref> It is well-suited for [[terrarium]]s, [[hanging basket]]s, and tabletop displays due to its compact size and visually appealing foliage.{{Short description|Species of flowering plant}}
